Project Title
TrustLens: AI-Powered scam, fraud, and fake job detection Platform

1. Introduction
The increasing use of online recruitment platforms, social media, and digital communication channels has led to a significant rise in recruitment-related cyber fraud. Fake job postings, fraudulent recruiters, phishing emails, fake internship offers, and impersonation websites target students and job seekers, resulting in financial losses, identity theft, and reduced trust in digital hiring processes.
TrustLens is a web-based platform designed to detect recruitment fraud, verify recruiters and companies, assess website legitimacy, and provide trust intelligence through AI-assisted analysis, cybersecurity checks, and community-driven reporting.

2. Problem Statement
Job seekers and educational institutions currently lack a centralized system for validating employment opportunities and identifying fraudulent recruitment activities.
Existing solutions focus on isolated aspects such as phishing detection or website analysis and do not provide a unified platform for recruitment fraud prevention.
The project aims to develop a trust intelligence platform that combines cybersecurity analysis, AI-powered reasoning, reputation management, and community reporting to improve trust in digital recruitment ecosystems.

3. Objectives
Primary Objectives
Detect fraudulent job postings and internship opportunities.


Verify the authenticity of recruiters and companies.


Identify phishing and scam recruitment communications.


Evaluate the trustworthiness of company websites.


Build a centralized repository of reported recruitment fraud cases.


Assist users in reporting suspicious recruitment activities.


Provide explainable risk assessments using AI.


Secondary Objectives
Support universities and placement cells in screening recruiters.


Reduce financial and identity theft risks for job seekers.


Generate recruitment fraud intelligence and trend analysis.


Establish a trusted recruitment verification ecosystem.



4. Scope of the Project
The system will provide:
Job posting analysis


Recruiter verification


Company verification


Website trust assessment


Scam communication analysis


Fraud intelligence repository


Similarity-based scam detection


Community reporting


Institutional dashboards


Fraud reporting assistance


The project will focus on recruitment-related fraud and will not handle financial fraud detection unrelated to hiring activities.

5. Stakeholders
Primary Stakeholders
Students


Job seekers


Universities


Placement cells


Recruitment agencies


Corporate HR departments


Job portals


Secondary Stakeholders
Government employment initiatives


Career counseling centers


Cybersecurity organizations



6. Functional Requirements
Module 1: Job Fraud Detection
The system shall:
Accept job descriptions and recruitment messages.


Detect unrealistic salary offers.


Detect advance-fee scams.


Identify suspicious hiring patterns.


Generate fraud risk scores.


Inputs
Job description text


Internship advertisements


Recruitment emails


LinkedIn opportunities


Outputs
Risk score


Risk category


Detailed explanation



Module 2: Recruiter Verification
The system shall:
Verify recruiter email domains.


Compare recruiter details with company information.


Check recruiter reputation history.


Display recruiter trust ratings.



Module 3: Company Verification
The system shall:
Verify company websites.


Analyze domain ownership information.


Check domain age.


Validate SSL certificates.


Generate company trust scores.



Module 4: Website Trust Assessment
The system shall:
Perform WHOIS analysis.


Validate SSL certificates.


Inspect security headers.


Detect typosquatting attempts.


Detect brand impersonation risks.



Module 5: Scam Communication Analyzer
The system shall analyze:
Emails


SMS messages


WhatsApp messages


Telegram messages


The system shall identify:
Phishing attempts


Credential theft attempts


Payment scams


Social engineering techniques



Module 6: Trust Intelligence Repository
The system shall maintain records of:
Verified companies


Suspicious companies


Recruiters


Fraud reports


Scam websites


Reported job postings


The system shall provide search and lookup functionality.

Module 7: Scam Similarity Detection
The system shall:
Compare incoming reports against historical scam data.


Identify similar fraud campaigns.


Display similarity percentages.


Suggest previously reported related cases.



Module 8: Community Reporting System
Users shall be able to:
Report fraudulent recruiters.


Report fake companies.


Report scam websites.


Upload supporting evidence.


Administrators shall review and validate reports.

Module 9: Institutional Dashboard
Placement officers shall be able to:
View approved companies.


View high-risk organizations.


Monitor complaint statistics.


Generate reports.


Track recruitment fraud trends.



Module 10: Fraud Reporting Assistance
The system shall:
Generate evidence reports.


Generate complaint summaries.


Export reports as PDF.


Provide guidance for reporting to official cybercrime portals.


Module 11 Recruitment Knowledge & Threat Intelligence RAG
Purpose
Provide evidence-backed answers using a curated knowledge base instead of relying only on LLM knowledge.
Knowledge Sources
Historical scam reports


Reported recruiters


Company risk registry


Verified company database


Cybersecurity guidelines


Recruitment fraud case studies


Government advisories


University placement records



7. Advanced Features
Recruitment Trust Graph
The system shall establish relationships among:
Companies


Recruiters


Domains


Websites


Job postings


Fraud reports


The graph shall help identify hidden scam networks.

Scam Campaign Detection
The system shall:
Group similar scams into campaigns.


Detect recurring scam patterns.


Identify emerging recruitment fraud trends.



Offer Letter Analysis
The system shall:
Analyze uploaded offer letters.


Detect suspicious clauses.


Identify inconsistencies.


Flag possible forged documents.



10. Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)
SDG 4 – Quality Education
Protects students from recruitment fraud and promotes cybersecurity awareness.
SDG 8 – Decent Work and Economic Growth
Encourages access to legitimate employment opportunities.
SDG 9 – Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure
Enhances trust and security in digital recruitment infrastructure.
SDG 16 – Peace, Justice and Strong Institutions
Supports fraud prevention, transparency, and safer online interactions.

Expected Outcome
TrustLens will provide a centralized recruitment fraud intelligence platform capable of detecting fake jobs, verifying recruiters and companies, analyzing suspicious communications, maintaining a trust repository, and supporting universities and job seekers in making informed recruitment decisions. This will improve trust, reduce fraud exposure, and contribute to safer digital hiring ecosystems.

Unique selling points

Recruitment Trust Intelligence Repository


Recruitment Trust Graph Analysis


Scam Similarity Detection System


Fraud Campaign Detection Engine


Placement Cell Intelligence Dashboard

